SDE WM: antialiased caption buttons and paddings that follow the title font.

Caption buttons (0.2.0 Alpha 2, audit A1-39): next to its 1-bit XBM masks a
theme may ship 8-bit masks as PNG pictures, named like them (close.png,
close_hover.png, max_toggled.png, max_hover_toggled.png, ...): any color on
transparent, square and larger than the buttons. Each state's picture is the
mask tinted with the state's image.color (window.active.button.*.image.color
as before) and is scaled with the button, whose size follows the title height
(window.button.*.percent), so the disc and the glyphs stay smooth from 100 %
to 200 %. A missing state falls back like the XBM masks; without
<button>.png a button keeps its XBM masks. Stock Openbox ignores the
pictures (and the keys below), so SDE themes still load there.

New themerc keys:
  padding.width.percent    padding.width, in percent of the title font height
  padding.height.percent   padding.height, likewise (the theme's padding.width
                           and padding.height stay the minimum)
SDE scales the title font with the interface, so the title bar, its buttons
and the menus' paddings grow with it instead of keeping 100 % paddings.

